        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T21:42:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I recently added logic that ensures that \"ecosystem interval\" is set when LE Audio connection is in progress, and also specified connection parameters as a range, not fixed value, that gives controller some room to decide what exact value to use.\n\nIf A2DP or HFP streaming is in progress, the minimum value we allowed, even for HID connection was 11.25ms . This value was chosen experimentally, and was as in stack at least 8 years ago. If there is no good reason, we probably shouldn\u0027t abandon it.\n\nThere is also extra handling for HID devices, to ensure they work smoothly with LE Audio devices.\n\n\nBased on above, I don\u0027t think going all the way down to 7.5-10ms for initial connection is good, even if you do it just for 1st or 2nd connection. how about 10-20, or 20-30ms instead ? This should be a big improvement.",
      "revId": "25ea7b7c799dc1064c7259ae0e3b9517a5dd1f17",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
